    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "title",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "not-just-a-gadget-but-a-rescue-mission-3",
      },
      "tag": "h2",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "not-just-a-gadget-but-a-rescue-mission-3",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "Not just a gadget, but a rescue mission",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "alt": "Snapchat Spectacles",
    "caption": "",
    "component": "image",
    "credit": "(Image credit: Future)",
    "errors": [],
    "html": "",
    "id": undefined,
    "imageurl": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Gc2ybUgdzM4RQrkhHZeWT5.jpg",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p id="elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa">It’s fair to say that the devices we use around us disconnect us from our surroundings, so Spiegel sees Specs as a “prison break” from the 7-hour-a-day screen habit that has been over 12 years in the making.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>“The biggest problem I see today is that people are spending seven or eight hours a day on their computer. We have to change that,” Spiegel commented. He calls it a “single player” experience that is a “disaster for our society” in pulling us away from one another.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>And it’s this that drove the philosophy that AR is the only human path. “Holding this tiny little screen in your hands was not the future of computers,” Spiegel proclaimed. Neither does he think it’s VR, as he bluntly critiqued this as “insane” and like “wearing a TV on your face.”</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "alt": "Snapchat Spectacles",
    "caption": "",
    "component": "image",
    "credit": "(Image credit: Future)",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "alt": "Snapchat Spectacles",
        "class": "inline",
        "data-new-v2-image": "true",
        "data-original-mos": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/jveTgBacuzPXXeMSd7WZbb.gif",
        "data-pin-media": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/jveTgBacuzPXXeMSd7WZbb.gif",
        "loading": "lazy",
        "src": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/jveTgBacuzPXXeMSd7WZbb.gif",
      },
      "tag": "img",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "height": undefined,
    "imageurl": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/jveTgBacuzPXXeMSd7WZbb.gif",
    "warnings": [],
    "width": undefined,
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "elk-2ec30f13-faea-4a31-bb96-20a256c076b0",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "elk-2ec30f13-faea-4a31-bb96-20a256c076b0",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p id="elk-2ec30f13-faea-4a31-bb96-20a256c076b0">In my time testing the developer versions of Specs, you can start to see this vision of taking that isolating layer of computing out and allowing us to reconnect. The Waveguide displays overlay your world with information and AI-driven context in ways that are actually useful, such as recipes and cooking steps, labeling items in front of you, or live subtitling people speaking around you.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "errors": [],
    "text": "<p>Sign up to get the BEST of Tom's Guide direct to your inbox.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "newsletter-form__strapline",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="newsletter-form__strapline">Get instant access to breaking news, the hottest reviews, great deals and helpful tips.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "errors": [],
    "text": "<p>Contact me with news and offers from other Future brands</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "errors": [],
    "text": "<p>Receive email from us on behalf of our trusted partners or sponsors</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "footer",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "newsletter-form__footer",
      },
      "tag": "footer",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "By submitting your information you agree to the <a href="https://futureplc.com/terms-conditions/" target="_blank">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> and <a href="https://futureplc.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank">Privacy Policy</a> and are aged 16 or over.",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>But how much are<em> </em>we <em>actually</em> reconnecting? This is something I found while <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/smart-glasses/i-zoned-out-and-stopped-listening-to-my-fiancee-and-the-even-realities-g2-made-sure-she-never-knew">testing the Even Realities G2</a> — finding that I may have looked physically present in the moment, but not really at the same time. My abilities to think critically and listen actively were being replaced by AI features like Conversate.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>Don’t get me wrong. This hands-off and eyes-on approach is definitely a step forward from always looking down at a screen, but real attention needs to be paid to software and app design to ensure that this isn’t all just for show.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "title",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "meta-s-camouflage-critique-3",
      },
      "tag": "h2",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "meta-s-camouflage-critique-3",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "Meta’s “camouflage” critique",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "alt": "Ray-Ban Meta Smart glasses",
    "caption": "",
    "component": "image",
    "credit": "(Image credit: Future)",
    "errors": [],
    "html": "",
    "id": undefined,
    "imageurl": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ZMnLQAX8D4hd8Dtgggi7En.jpg",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "elk-dec27555-b7a3-4f0a-9203-4fab6a6b8c43",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "elk-dec27555-b7a3-4f0a-9203-4fab6a6b8c43",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p id="elk-dec27555-b7a3-4f0a-9203-4fab6a6b8c43">Spiegel also offered a sharp take on Meta’s partnership with Luxottica (the company behind Ray-Ban) — saying that Meta had to partner with a fashion brand to remove the liability of its own brand name.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "errors": [],
    "text": "<p>What to read next</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "flex flex-col gap-0 m-0",
      },
      "tag": "ul",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<ul class="flex flex-col gap-0 m-0"> <li> <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/smart-glasses/i-swapped-my-ray-ban-metas-for-these-usd20-smart-glasses-just-to-mock-them-then-they-actually-impressed-me" class="flex gap-2 items-center no-underline text-inherit flex-row-reverse"> <span>I swapped my Ray-Ban Metas for these $20 smart glasses just to mock them — then they actually impressed me</span> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/smart-glasses/ive-been-wearing-the-meta-ray-ban-display-smart-glasses-for-24-hours-heres-what-i-like-and-hate" class="flex gap-2 items-center no-underline text-inherit flex-row-reverse"> <span>I've been wearing the Meta Ray-Ban Display smart glasses for 24 hours — here's what I like (and hate)</span> </a> </li> <li> <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/smart-glasses/i-fed-my-tamagotchi-looked-like-a-d1-athlete-and-fact-checked-my-boss-my-time-with-even-g2s-secret-smart-glasses-app-store" class="flex gap-2 items-center no-underline text-inherit flex-row-reverse"> <span>I fed my Tamagotchi, looked like a D1 athlete and fact-checked my boss — my time with Even G2's secret smart glasses app store</span> </a> </li> </ul>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>"I think Meta really needed to partner with Luxottica because the Meta brand I think is not something that people want to put anywhere near their face,” Spiegel commented. “"What's challenging for Luxottica is they took like the most iconic, crazy high-margin product and they destroyed the margin and then they associated it with Meta.”</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>It’s an interesting point, and one that after seeing <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/social-media/metas-new-digital-afterlife-patent-is-the-most-black-mirror-thing-ive-ever-seen-i-want-to-be-remembered-not-replicated">Meta filing a patent to digitally resurrect its users</a>, and getting <a href="https://www.engadget.com/big-tech/meta-warned-by-dozens-of-organizations-that-facial-recognition-on-its-smart-glasses-would-empower-predators-185000998.html" target="_blank">warned by organizations</a> to not turn on facial recognition in smart glasses, I can kind of see the sense in. A lot of my friends and family have a love/hate relationship with Meta in its connected platforms vs invasion of privacy, so to put Luxottica names on its camera-equipped hardware is a smart move.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "alt": "Snapchat Spectacles",
    "caption": "",
    "component": "image",
    "credit": "(Image credit: Future)",
    "errors": [],
    "html": "",
    "id": undefined,
    "imageurl": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/28khS6RTnkxJKuM6QcBPf3.jpg",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "elk-6028c3ae-2661-4d69-8bfd-f658b69634cf",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": "elk-6028c3ae-2661-4d69-8bfd-f658b69634cf",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p id="elk-6028c3ae-2661-4d69-8bfd-f658b69634cf">But the Snap Specs will be in a different direction — built and designed in house. “Control of the hardware is necessary to deliver an extraordinary customer experience,” Spiegel added.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>When <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/smart-glasses/exclusive-i-asked-snaps-hardware-chief-about-the-companys-next-gen-specs-heres-what-i-found-out">speaking to the former VP of hardware, Scott Myers</a>, it’s clear that form factor is a priority for the company, as he emphasized that “the social acceptability element is so critically important.”</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>Quite how the company manages to pull this off with the vast amounts of compute and sensor tech required to pull off the Specs without a puck is going to be a monumental challenge. But I’m curious to see!</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "alt": "Google News",
    "caption": "",
    "component": "image",
    "credit": "",
    "errors": [],
    "html": "",
    "id": undefined,
